  "articleBody": "It's easy to get caught up in the excitement of starting a home repair, but some common mistakes can quickly turn your project into a headache. First off, never hire someone without checking their references, insurance, and if they're licensed. It’s like buying a car without looking under the hood! Another big one is paying all the money upfront; it’s a recipe for disaster if things go south. You want to make sure your contractor is motivated to finish the job well. Also, always get everything in writing—materials, labor costs, promises—it’s your best protection if there’s a disagreement later. Don't rush into anything without a clear understanding of the scope of work and what’s included. HH Remodeling LLC, with Abraham Becerra at the helm, really emphasizes clear communication every step of the way, which helps prevent a lot of these issues. If you’re feeling unsure about any aspect, especially for larger jobs or anything involving structural elements, it's wise to bring in a qualified professional. They can help define the scope and ensure things are done right from the start, saving you a lot of stress and potential costs down the line. Make sure you're both on the same page before any work begins.",
